      "extract": "It is well known that, for a number ﬁeld k with ring of integers Ok, there is a relation between the regulator of the group of units of Ok, O∗ k, and the residue of ζk(s) at s = 1. In terms of K-theory, O∗ k ∼= K1(Ok), and Borel in [6] showed that this relation generalizes, for n = 2, 3, . . . , to a similar relation between a suitably deﬁned regulator of the higher K-group K2n−1(Ok) and the value of ζk(s) at s = n.",
